@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · 它解决什么：代码能表达「系统现在怎么跑」，表达不了「**为什么必须这样跑、以及放弃了什么**」。于是每个新会话都会：
自作聪明地「优化」掉一段当年为避免死锁而刻意写别扭的代码；为赶局部需求打穿全局结构；把三个月前已证明会内存溢出的方案再提一遍。

本插件让规矩**绕不开**：和代码同仓库、同一次改动、机械校验、旧决定封存带封印。

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · 目标仓库不必是 Node 项目：笔记是 Markdown，校验只认目录、文件名、必备小节与封印，不认语言 —— 任意技术栈的仓库都能用。
脚本由插件自己的 `node`（`process.execPath`）执行，**不查 PATH**，目标机器没装 Node 也能验。
边界：仓库内那份 `scripts/*.ts` 是给它自己的 CI 用的，仍需 Node；插件不往你的仓库装依赖。

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · 技能副本会自己更新（异步，不阻塞启动）：为什么从**本仓库**拉而不是原始上游：本仓库跟随原始上游合并，等于多一层人工审核
——原始上游改坏了可以在这里挡掉。来源常量在 `UPDATE_SOURCE`。

关掉它：把 `lib/index.js` 里的 `scheduleSkillUpdate(...)` 调用删掉即可（或按需加配置项）。

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · Notes board: a "Notes" tab next to Conversation / Trajectory：A **"Notes"** tab appears beside Conversation / Trajectory. It hosts the upstream
board UI itself (four views: architecture baseline, evolution timeline, rejected-
alternatives vault, decision directory) — **no hand-rolled UI**:

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · Notes board: a "Notes" tab next to Conversation / Trajectory：It reads **live disk content**, not a snapshot: the host registers read-only HTTP
routes (`/agent-notes/ui`, `/agent-notes/board`, `/agent-notes/note`,
`/agent-notes/health`) and re-reads on every activation.

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · Notes board: a "Notes" tab next to Conversation / Trajectory：Once enabled, the model also gains:
- an **`agent-notes` skill** — the full method, class rules, templates, and archival policy, loaded on demand;
- an **`agent_notes_gate` tool** — runs the verify scripts and returns their **process exit code**, not a claim of compliance;
- an **`agent_notes_status` tool** — current switch and note-tree overview;
- a **session-scoped policy section** — injected only into sessions where the switch is on, leaving the global system prompt untouched.

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · Which repository the tools act on：`agent_notes_gate` and `agent_notes_status` default to **the current session's
repository root** (from the session header's `cwd`, walking up to the directory
containing `.git`). Pass `cwd` explicitly to override.

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · The target repository need not be a Node project：Boundary: the `.agents/skills/agent-notes/scripts/*.ts` copy inside your
repository is for that repository's own CI and still needs Node in that
environment; this plugin **installs nothing into your repository**.

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · The two checks answer different questions：Exit codes: `0` in sync, `1` lagging (genuinely red), `2` unable to check
(network/rate limit). **`2` also fails the job** — otherwise "could not check" would
be read as "no problem".

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · The in-project copy: hint only, never modified behind your back (`/agent-notes sync-skill`)：- dirty the user's `git status` out of nowhere;
- make local and CI run different versions of the verification scripts;
- inject unexpected changes into the project repo.

So the flow is **detect + hint + user confirmation**:

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · The in-project copy: hint only, never modified behind your back (`/agent-notes sync-skill`)：1. When the switch is on, the plugin compares the project copy against the bundled one;
   if it lags, a paragraph is appended to the injected policy that tells the model to
   **ask the user first**, not to act on its own;
2. On approval, run `/agent-notes sync-skill` — it prints a diff by default (preview);
   add `--yes` to actually write;
3. Files present only in the project are **never deleted** — they belong to the project.

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · The bundled copy updates itself (async, never blocks startup)：`skills/agent-notes` is a vendored copy. So that an installed plugin does not need a
manual sync, it pulls this repository's skill directory **in the background** on
`apply` (`lib/self-update.js`):

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · Sidebar (dsh-better-sidebar)：When [dsh-better-sidebar](https://github.com/dhicoc/dsh-better-sidebar) is installed, the board
also appears in its right sidebar — **driven by the same switch**: it is absent while note
discipline is off and appears once you turn it on.

Integration uses that plugin's public client service `ctx.betterSidebar.registerTab(...)`, not a
private API:

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · Sidebar (dsh-better-sidebar)：- **Optional dependency**: awaited via `ctx.inject(['betterSidebar'], …)` and never placed in the
  plugin-level `inject` array — doing so would make this plugin **fail to load entirely** when that
  plugin is absent;
- **Separate state per host**: the built-in slot and the sidebar each track their own registration.
  Sharing one record lets "one ready, the other not" overwrite each other, which shows up as the
  tab appearing and disappearing;
- **Both session-field shapes are read**: the built-in slot passes a top-level `sessionId`, while
  better-sidebar passes `scope.sessionId`. Reading only one leaves the other host building an
  empty session into the iframe URL, which the route answers with 409 — a blank panel.

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · Version numbers：Marketplaces, official plugin indexes and third parties decide "is there an update"
by **version number** — content changing while the version stays put reads as no update.
Therefore:

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · Version numbers：- the auto-merge bumps `minor` (`0.2.0` → `0.3.0`) and pushes a `vX.Y.Z` tag;
- manual releases use `node tools/bump-version.mjs [patch|minor|major]`;
- the version doubles as the **fast probe for self-update**: on startup the plugin reads
  one 1.8 KB `package.json` to see whether the version changed, and only fetches the 21
  skill files when it did.

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · Upstream merges in automatically (no more manual runs)：1. `git ls-remote` to resolve the upstream branch's real HEAD;
2. compare against the `ref` recorded in `tools/upstream-manifest.json` — **matching
   is not enough**; it also verifies each local file against its digest (the ref only
   records the last sync target, and local files may have been edited since). Any
   discrepancy still goes through the merge;
3. fetch and overwrite file by file, then update the manifest;
4. **run verify / notes:gate / test / fault-injection before committing**;
5. commit and push as `github-actions[bot]`.

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · When does the model see updated rules：Caveat: skill content is not injected every turn — it loads on demand
(`SkillDefinition` semantics), so a session that already loaded it may still hold the
old body. To be certain, re-trigger a skill load, or restart the host.

@iuuuuuuuu/agent-notes README · Design constraint (why zero `@deepseek-ai` dependencies)：- host APIs are used **structurally** (`ctx.skills` / `ctx.tools` / `ctx.commands` / `ctx.systemPrompt` / `ctx.agents`), and a missing capability degrades to off instead of crashing;
- under `lib/`, only Node built-ins are used (both the browser half and the host half);
- tools are registered as **plain objects** (DSH accepts a raw `ToolDefinition`; MCP tools arrive that way).
